import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 461 | Dragon Ball · Frieza Army: The Extreme Form of Predatory Civilization","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 461 | Dragon Ball · Frieza Army: The Extreme Form of Predatory Civilization","no":461,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Frieza Army","Predatory Civilization","Extreme Form","Anti-Predation"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","47-Anti-Monopoly Law"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0461_模块2-龙珠-弗利萨军团-掠夺式文明的极端形态.md","filePath":"en/0461_模块2-龙珠-弗利萨军团-掠夺式文明的极端形态.md"}'),r={name:"en/0461_模块2-龙珠-弗利萨军团-掠夺式文明的极端形态.md"};function o(s,e,l,d,u,c){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-461-dragon-ball-·-frieza-army-the-extreme-form-of-predatory-civilization" tabindex="-1">Entry 461 | Dragon Ball · Frieza Army: The Extreme Form of Predatory Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-461-dragon-ball-·-frieza-army-the-extreme-form-of-predatory-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 461 | Dragon Ball · Frieza Army: The Extreme Form of Predatory Civilization&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 30 · Civilization Analysis 3) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 19, 47</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-predation-becomes-an-industry" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when predation becomes an industry <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-predation-becomes-an-industry" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when predation becomes an industry&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Frieza Army is Dragon Ball worldview&#39;s extreme form of &quot;predatory civilization&quot;: it is not just a villain organization, but an <strong>interstellar predation industry</strong> — hiring Saiyans to conquer planets, selling natives as slaves, shipping resources back to Frieza&#39;s homeworld. It has organization, hierarchy, business model; it is Dragon Ball world&#39;s most mature &quot;civilization&quot; — unfortunately predatory. This entry takes the <strong>anti-predation axiom</strong> as core, dissecting the Frieza Army&#39;s predatory structure.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Frieza Army&#39;s energy waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Predation replaces construction</strong>: the army&#39;s entire &quot;energy&quot; used for conquest and trafficking; never builds any conquered planet</li><li><strong>Frieza&#39;s personal energy waste</strong>: Frieza was a genius rare in ten thousand years, yet put all talent into &quot;maintaining army rule,&quot; not opening new cultivation paths</li><li><strong>Subordinate race talent wasted</strong>: Ginyu Force, Dodoria, Zarbon these subordinates, each with talent, yet locked in &quot;Frieza&#39;s thug&quot; position</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Frieza Army as predatory civilization&#39;s regression inevitability:</p><ol><li><strong>Stock exhausted</strong>: living by conquering planets; one conquest one less; ultimately the conquered unite and overthrow</li><li><strong>Internal corruption</strong>: army maintained by fear; Frieza falls and the whole system instantly collapses</li><li><strong>No technological spillover</strong>: conquered planets&#39; technology and culture plundered empty, but these looted resources only used to maintain the army, not to feed back</li><li><strong>Conclusion</strong>: predatory civilization&#39;s fate is being overthrown by the conquered — Frieza&#39;s ending is precisely this fate</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking in his relationship with the Frieza Army:</p><ul><li><strong>Beating Frieza but not reforming</strong>: after Goku beats Frieza, he never pushes &quot;how to rebuild the hundred planets under Frieza Army control&quot; — he leaves after fighting, leaving ruins</li><li><strong>Frieza revived and fought again</strong>: in Super Frieza revives; Goku fights again — predatory-civilization problem never institutionally solved, just repeated in a different way</li><li><strong>No responsibility for subordinate races</strong>: Frieza Army subordinate races (Ginyu Force, Dodoria, Zarbon) in narrative are only &quot;thugs&quot;; Goku never cares about these races being coerced by Frieza</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Frieza Predatory Civilization</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conquer planets, sell natives</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republicanism: any race equal; conquest not a trade</td></tr><tr><td>Frieza personal dictatorship</td><td>Anchor Council + separation of powers; not tied to one person</td></tr><tr><td>Subordinate race talent wasted</td><td>Five Myriad-Ranks genealogies equal; each shows strengths</td></tr><tr><td>Conquered planets no rebuilding</td><td>Anti-predation axiom: develop increment, do not consume stock</td></tr><tr><td>Fear maintains rule</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republican co-build: order by consensus, not fear</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Frieza Army structure — from hiring Saiyans to being overthrown by Goku</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;if Frieza Army took Myriad-Ranks republican route, changed conquest to co-build&quot; control</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count conquered planets&#39; survival years, subordinate race talent-utilization rate, Frieza Army civilization survival time</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Frieza Predatory-Civilization Collapse Report</em>, quantifying &quot;predatory civilization&#39;s inevitable ending&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Frieza Army setting self-consistency: medium</strong> (army structure broadly self-consistent in Namek arc; late Frieza revival, Golden Frieza, Black Frieza layers added)</li><li><strong>Predatory-civilization self-consistency: low</strong> — predatory civilization itself cannot long-term be self-consistent</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong> (Frieza repeatedly revived in original, Super, Heroes; each revival &quot;four months of training&quot; and catches up to Goku)</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high</strong> — Frieza Army&#39;s collapse all by Goku; no institutional solution</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: predation replaces construction; energy for conquest not co-build</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Frieza Army is predatory civilization&#39;s extreme form; anti-predation axiom&#39;s reverse specimen</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least broke internal predation; Frieza Army is institutionalized interstellar predation</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: conquered planets, subordinate races in narrative all backdrop</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: predatory civilization cannot truly expand; only consumes stock until collapse</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Frieza Army is Dragon Ball worldview&#39;s mirror for all &quot;predatory civilizations&quot;: it has organization, hierarchy, business model, but its fate is being overthrown by the conquered. Goku beat Frieza, but did not shatter the &quot;predator—prey&quot; structure itself — Frieza revives, Golden Frieza, Black Frieza; the problem repeats again and again. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer: beating the predator is not enough; must shatter predatory structure itself. Let Myriad Ranks no longer live by being conquered; this is the Frieza Army&#39;s true lesson to Dragon Ball world.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · Frieza Army · the extreme form of predatory civilization described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./460_模块2-龙珠-赛亚人设定-战斗民族的掠夺本质.html">Entry 460 · Saiyan Setting</a> · <a href="./462_模块2-龙珠-女子角色处境-布尔玛等角色的工具化.html">Entry 462 · Women Characters&#39; Situation</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const y=i(r,[["render",o]]);export{g as __pageData,y as default};
